==Evolution==
Evolves into '''One Two Three ~ Hara Idols Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Idol Mihara & Cat''' after completing [[Hiroshi Mihara Awakens!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Hiroshi simply lacks the stats to be an effective anti-Floating. While he does have [[Area Attack]], decent uptime, and a good proc chance, especially in his [[True Form]], his garishly long cooldown time prevents him from being stacked like [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]]. What sounds like an easy task of stacking three Hiroshis to solve this actually takes more than a minute with no survivability to boot. All in all, Necro-Dancer and [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] run laps around Hiroshi as they are much more spammable and sustainable.

